RF.put("questb:b72",{"8632":{"id":8632,"t":"Enigma Circlet","lv":60,"min":60,"side":"Both","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Bring Vek'nilash's Circlet, 2 Idols of Night, 5 Bronze Scarabs and 5 Ivory Scarabs to Andorgos in Ahn'Qiraj. You must also attain Friendly reputation with the Brood of Nozdormu to complete this quest.\nVek'nilash's Circlet Emperor Vek'nilash in Ahn'Qiraj Temple\n2 Idol of Night Vekniss Soldier 0.5 % in Ahn'Qiraj Temple , Vekniss Warrior 0.5 % in Ahn'Qiraj Temple , Vekniss Guardian 0.5 % in Ahn'Qiraj Temple , Vekniss Stinger 0.5 % in Ahn'Qiraj Temple and 4 more\n5 Bronze Scarab Flesh Hunter 1 % in Ruins of Ahn'Qiraj , Vekniss Soldier 1 % in Ahn'Qiraj Temple , Vekniss Warrior 1 % in Ahn'Qiraj Temple , Vekniss Guardian 1 % in Ahn'Qiraj Temple and 4 more\n5 Ivory Scarab Flesh Hunter 1 % in Ruins of Ahn'Qiraj , Vekniss Soldier 1 % in Ahn'Qiraj Temple , Vekniss Warrior 1 % in Ahn'Qiraj Temple , Vekniss Guardian 1 % in Ahn'Qiraj Temple and 4 more\nReach 3000 reputation with Brood of Nozdormu","desc":"The Twin Emperors... their incessant whispers are slowly taking a toll on my sanity. They mock me, knowing I cannot step further into their domain to save my brother Arygos.\nIn my visions I see their monstrous faces adorned by powerful crowns. But I will have my revenge... I will transmute these symbols of Qiraji power to ones better suited to our needs.\nBring me the components I require, ‹name›. I will give you a headpiece of unmatched power.","rew":"You will receive:\nEnigma Circlet\nExperience: 9,950\n+200 reputation with Brood of Nozdormu","back":"Did you bring me the components I asked for, ‹name›?","done":"You've succeeded! The whispers from the Twin Emperors have ceased.\nTake this as a reward. The mere sight of it will strike fear in the hearts of the Qiraji... it shall remind them of their fallen leaders and of the mortal that slew them.\nStart Andorgos Ahn'Qiraj Temple End Andorgos Ahn'Qiraj Temple Level 60 , requires level 60 Difficulty 60 Side Both factions Class Mage Type Raid Shareable Yes Repeatable Yes Quest ID 8632\nThe chain\n2 quests at level 60, 16,550 XP in all.\n1 [ 60 ] Mortal Champions\nKandrostrasz Ahn'Qiraj Temple\n6,600 XP\n2 [ 60 ] Enigma Circlet this quest\nBring Vek'nilash's Circlet, 2 Idols of Night, 5 Bronze Scarabs and 5 Ivory Scarabs to Andorgos in Ahn'Qiraj.\nAndorgos Ahn'Qiraj Temple\n9,950 XP","cats":["ahnqiraj"]},"8712":{"id":8712,"t":"Scythe of the Unseen Path","lv":60,"min":60,"side":"Both","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Bring 1 Qiraji Spiked Hilt, 2 Azure Idols, 5 Silver Scarabs and 5 Bone Scarabs to Warden Haro in Silithus. You must also attain Exalted reputation with Cenarion Circle to complete this quest.\nQiraji Spiked Hilt Ossirian the Unscarred 40 % in Ruins of Ahn'Qiraj , Moam 40 % in Ruins of Ahn'Qiraj , Ayamiss the Hunter 10 % in Ruins of Ahn'Qiraj , Buru the Gorger 10 % in Ruins of Ahn'Qiraj\n2 Azure Idol Flesh Hunter 10 % in Ruins of Ahn'Qiraj , Hive'Zara Drone 0.5 % in Ruins of Ahn'Qiraj , Hive'Zara Collector 0.5 % in Ruins of Ahn'Qiraj , Hive'Zara Soldier 0.5 % in Ruins of Ahn'Qiraj and 4 more\n5 Silver Scarab Flesh Hunter 1 % in Ruins of Ahn'Qiraj , Vekniss Soldier 1 % in Ahn'Qiraj Temple , Vekniss Warrior 1 % in Ahn'Qiraj Temple , Vekniss Guardian 1 % in Ahn'Qiraj Temple and 4 more\n5 Bone Scarab Flesh Hunter 1 % in Ruins of Ahn'Qiraj , Vekniss Soldier 1 % in Ahn'Qiraj Temple , Vekniss Warrior 1 % in Ahn'Qiraj Temple , Vekniss Guardian 1 % in Ahn'Qiraj Temple and 4 more\nReach 42000 reputation with Cenarion Circle","desc":"The Qiraji and their servants wield items made with the rarest and finest materials: bones from gargantuan ancient creatures, gems from the depths of the earth, metals pure and strong.\nJust the sight of Qiraji artifacts fills me with an urge to practice my craft with their shattered and smelted pieces. Prove your allegiance to the Circle, ‹name›, and I will make you a powerful weapon from the finest Qiraji materials.","rew":"You will receive:\nScythe of the Unseen Path\nExperience: 6,600\n+100 reputation with Cenarion Circle","back":"Did you bring me the components I require, ‹name›?","done":"You've done well, ‹class›. This is a masterwork hilt... the balance is perfect.\nTake your weapon, ‹name›. Wield it with great confidence and vanquish our enemies!","pins":[{"z":"Silithus","x":51.1,"y":38.9,"n":"Warden Haro","e":1,"s":1}],"cats":["ahnqiraj"]},"8792":{"id":8792,"t":"The Horde Needs Your Help!","lv":60,"min":1,"side":"Horde","tag":"changed","st":"Changed in Forever. Requires level 1 instead of 10.","obj":"Speak with Warlord Gorchuk in Orgrimmar's Valley of Spirits.","desc":"Hello, I'm glad that you've decided to hear me out. The Horde needs all of the help that it can get to prepare for the Ahn'Qiraj War, and that means that we need you! Even now as we speak, official collectors are gathering the necessary material needed for the upcoming war, but we won't be able to meet our goals without your assistance, ‹name›!\nYou should go speak with the guy in charge, Warlord Gorchuk. What do you say, ‹class›? Will you help out with the vital preparations?","rew":"Experience: 650","done":"Throm'ka, ‹class›! Good to see so many of the Horde, such as yourself, ‹name›, coming out to lend your support in laying the groundwork for the upcoming Ahn'Qiraj War. The effort here will ensure that we are victorious against the Silithid and their evil masters hidden away inside Ahn'Qiraj.\nSo now that you are here, be sure to speak with the various collectors and offer your assistance in gathering those materials that you are suited to.\nThunder Bluff Orgrimmar","pins":[{"z":"Thunder Bluff","x":39.9,"y":51.7,"n":"Senior Sergeant Taiga","s":1},{"z":"Orgrimmar","x":29.8,"y":67.3,"n":"Warlord Gorchuk","e":1}],"cats":["ahnqiraj-war"]},"99192":{"id":99192,"t":"A donation of silk","lv":60,"min":26,"side":"Alliance","tag":"new","st":"New in Forever.","obj":"60 Silk Cloth\nLevel 60 , requires level 26 Difficulty 26 56 58 Side Alliance Quest ID 99192","cats":["alterac-mountains"]},"8392":{"id":8392,"t":"Claiming Arathi Basin","lv":49,"min":40,"side":"Alliance","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Bring 3 Arathi Basin Marks of Honor to an Alliance Brigadier General outside the battlegrounds.\n3 Arathi Basin Mark of Honor","desc":"Winning a war is about more than just outsmarting and outfighting your opponent. Victory often comes down to simply producing more than your enemy.\nWhat we have in Arathi Basin is a sizeable supply of resources for whichever side manages to claim it first.\nIf the Alliance comes out victorious, it'll mean more swords and pikes for our troops. If the Horde were to win, those swords and pikes would still get made, they'd just be pointed at us! Now is the time to help the Alliance in Arathi Basin, ‹name›.","rew":"Experience: 2,250\n+50 reputation with The League of Arathor","back":"Tell me, what are the news from the front?","done":"Good work, soldier! Keep it up and we'll have the Horde running all the way back to Orgrimmar.\nDun Morogh Darnassus Stormwind City","pins":[{"z":"Dun Morogh","x":62.3,"y":35.5,"n":"Alliance Brigadier General","e":1,"s":1},{"z":"Darnassus","x":58,"y":34.2,"n":"Alliance Brigadier General","e":1,"s":1},{"z":"Stormwind City","x":81.2,"y":38.5,"n":"Alliance Brigadier General","e":1,"s":1}],"cats":["arathi-basin"]},"92872":{"id":92872,"t":"Dutiful steps","lv":38,"min":32,"side":"Alliance","tag":"new","st":"New in Forever.","obj":"Throw the Pouch of Tomb Dust into The Great Sea and return to Caretaker Alaric in the Stromgarde Keep crypt.\nPouch of Tomb Dust thrown into the sea behind Stromgarde","desc":"We eternally guard this tomb and the knowledge of ceremonial rites used to honor these fallen souls.\nNow that you've descended three levels below the earth, you take your first steps toward returning to the sunlit world with sacred wisdom.\nEach season, we carry some of the dust from this tomb and spread it to the oceans of Azeroth. A symbolic act of renewing cycles.\nTake this small satchel. Travel to the cliffs behind Stromgarde Keep and cast it into the sea.\nLevel 38 , requires level 32 Difficulty 32 34 36 41 48 Side Alliance Quest ID 92872","cats":["arathi-highlands"]},"1032":{"id":1032,"t":"Satyr Slaying!","lv":32,"min":26,"side":"Alliance","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Bring 16 Satyr Horns to Illiyana in Forest Song.\n16 Satyr Horns Geltharis 50 % , Caedakar the Vicious 50 % , Balizar the Umbrage 50 % , Aligar the Tormentor 50 % and 4 more","desc":"I can't believe that Anilia is gone... We used to play together in the forests all the time. I almost feel... sad.\nI know something that might make me feel better. Please, slay the satyrs that took Anilia from me! Bring me their horns as proof of your actions and you will forever have my gratitude.","rew":"Money: 30 0 gold, 30 silver, 0 copper Experience: 2,550\n+100 reputation with Darnassus","back":"Please, help me avenge Anilia's death.","done":"Thank you, kind ‹race›. My sister's spirit is gladdened by your efforts.","pins":[{"z":"Ashenvale","x":21.7,"y":53.3,"n":"Illiyana","e":1,"s":1}],"cats":["ashenvale"]},"712":{"id":712,"t":"Study of the Elements: Rock","lv":42,"min":35,"side":"Both","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Bring 5 Bracers of Rock Binding to Lotwil Veriatus in the Badlands.\n5 Bracers of Rock Binding Greater Rock Elemental 80 %","desc":"‹name›, there's one more part I need from the elementals here in the Badlands: the bracers of rock binding from the greater rock elementals. By my calculations, those bracers should be enough to gauge the strength of my own shackles.\nMy attempts at scrying the greater rock elementals showed a group of them southwest of here, near some ogres if I recall.\nBring me 5 of their bracers just so I have extras. Servo's notorious for misplacing my reagents and research.","rew":"Experience: 3,450","back":"The stone slabs you found were ideal, ‹name›. Lucien will be taking the extra ones back to Kharanos when we're done here. After all, they could prove useful again.\nFor instance, they'd be a nice basis for a handy little shelter once I start looking into a multidisciplinary approach to high-yield explosives...","done":"‹name›, have you ever considered becoming a research assistant? No? I'm not sure what I'll do without your abilities here. Intelligence, curiosity, and strength--all combined into one package.","pins":[{"z":"Badlands","x":25.9,"y":44.9,"n":"Lotwil Veriatus","e":1,"s":1}],"cats":["badlands"]},"9032":{"id":9032,"t":"Bodley's Unfortunate Fate","lv":60,"min":58,"side":"Horde","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Travel to Blackrock Mountain and use the Extra-Dimensional Ghost Revealer to find Bodley near Blackrock Spire.","desc":"The medallion contained Valthalak's soul? It's no surprise it was guarded by such a powerful curse.\nLocating Bodley presents a bit of a problem. Last time I heard of him, he was preparing to venture back into Blackrock Spire. He was never heard of again.\nSeek him out in Blackrock Mountain, though I'm afraid to say he's probably dead by now. I suggest taking the goblin's device with you, friend.","rew":"Experience: 1,650","done":"I am so glad that you can see me. Finally someone to talk to!\nWill you help us, ‹name›? Help to undo the wrong that we perpetrated and put things to right? If it's true that you already have the Top Piece of Lord Valthalak's Amulet, then I think I can point you in the right direction to acquire the other two parts, reunite them and put an end to all of this.\nOh, by the way, hello, my name is Bodley. Nice to meet you!\nOrgrimmar Burning Steppes","pins":[{"z":"Orgrimmar","x":34.9,"y":38.3,"n":"Mokvar","s":1},{"z":"Burning Steppes","x":32.3,"y":25.8,"n":"Bodley","e":1}],"cats":["blackrock-mountain"]},"94232":{"id":94232,"t":"Craftsmans writ minor recombobulator","min":1,"side":"Both","tag":"new","st":"New in Forever. Its level is not known yet. Partly read from what players of our addon saw in game.","obj":"Acquire the items requested by the customer and deliver them to the location marked on your map. This writ must be in your possession to complete the transaction.\nCraftsman's Writ: Minor Recombobulator\nMinor Recombobulator","desc":"<Penned in faded ink, the note is requesting 1 Minor Recombobulator, along with information about delivery location and payment. At the bottom appears text denoting this writ is transferable.>","rew":"You will receive:\nCoin Pouch\n+75 reputation with Azeroth Commerce Authority\n+75 reputation with Durotar Supply and Logistics","back":"Do we have business?","done":"I don't know what I expected when I sent out an order for a curse dispelling device, but this Minor Recon--Racom--ugh, Minor Whatchamacallit sure ain't it!\nLook, I know how complicated the refund process is and I do NOT have time for that. It's way easier for us both if I just take this off your hands, and I'll be more specific with my next order.\nFor both of our sakes, let's hope you don't screw that one up too!","pins":[{"z":"Duskwood","x":81.7,"y":19.9,"n":"Kzixx","e":1}],"cats":["crafting"]},"94312":{"id":94312,"t":"Craftsmans writ orange martial shirt","min":1,"side":"Both","tag":"new","st":"New in Forever. Its level is not known yet.","obj":"Acquire the items requested by the customer and deliver them to the location marked on your map. This writ must be in your possession to complete the transaction.\nCraftsman's Writ: Orange Martial Shirt\nOrange Martial Shirt","desc":"<Penned in faded ink, the note is requesting $2oa Orange Martial Shirt, along with information about delivery location and payment. At the bottom appears text denoting this writ is transferable.>\nStart an item: Craftsman's Writ: Orange Martial Shirt Level 0 , requires level 1 Difficulty 1 3 Side Both factions Quest ID 94312","cats":["crafting"]},"7672":{"id":7672,"t":"Nightsaber Replacement","lv":1,"min":60,"side":"Alliance","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Reins of the Nightsaber","rew":"You will be able to choose one of these rewards:\nReins of the Swift Stormsaber Reins of the Swift Frostsaber Reins of the Swift Mistsaber","back":"[PH] If you bring me your old nightsaber, I will trade it in for one from the new pack. The new swift saber will be just as fast as your old one, but have a different look to it. You can look at the swift sabers we already have around the yard here to see what it will look like.","pins":[{"z":"Darnassus","x":38.3,"y":15.4,"n":"Lelanai","e":1,"s":1}],"cats":["darnassus"]},"952":{"id":952,"t":"Grove of the Ancients","lv":17,"min":6,"side":"Alliance","tag":"changed","st":"Changed in Forever. Level 17 instead of 11. Gives 1,250 experience instead of 875, 1.43 times as much.","obj":"Deliver Fandral's message to Onu in the Grove of the Ancients in Darkshore, south of Auberdine.\nFandral's Message\nProvided: Fandral's Message","desc":"If you had enough time to run messages for the Oracle Tree, then I'm sure that I can press you into service to deliver a message to the Grove of the Ancients in Darkshore, due south of Auberdine.\nYou will most likely have to secure transport on a hippogryph, but I have faith enough in you that you can manage that. Take this to Onu, the Ancient of Lore. He has been awaiting word from me, even as I waited for news from the Oracle Glade.","rew":"Experience: 1,250\n+100 reputation with Darnassus","back":"Ah. ‹class›. How may Onu assist you?","done":"Ah. Thank you, ‹name›. It is strange, though. The Arch Druid always seems in such a hurry. The forest knows that all shall come to pass in the appointed time. Shan'do Stormrage understood that.\nDarnassus Darkshore","pins":[{"z":"Darnassus","x":34.8,"y":9.3,"n":"Arch Druid Fandral Staghelm","s":1},{"z":"Darkshore","x":43.6,"y":76.3,"n":"Onu","e":1}],"cats":["darnassus"]},"94872":{"id":94872,"t":"Buying friendship magram","lv":45,"min":30,"side":"Both","tag":"new","st":"New in Forever.","obj":"Bring the Totem Tote to the Magram Quartermaster at Magram Village in the Desolace to significantly increase your reputation with that clan. You must be of at least Neutral standing with the Magram Clan Centaur.\nProvided: Totem Tote","desc":"The fierce Magram are undoubtedly winning the war of territories at the moment. While we can all be thankful the clashes haven't erupted too frequently throughout the desert, every day their village just to the east grows a little bigger; their soldiers a little bolder.\nI worry gravely about the consequences of an unchecked Magram clan, but I cannot deny their potential as an ally.\nIf you wish to earn their trust, offer this sack of totems to their quartermaster, but be careful.\nLevel 45 , requires level 30 Difficulty 30 41 43 48 57 Side Both factions Quest ID 94872","cats":["desolace"]},"312":{"id":312,"t":"Tundra MacGrann's Stolen Stash","lv":12,"min":7,"side":"Alliance","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Retrieve Tundra MacGrann's dried meats from the stolen meat locker in Old Icebeard's cave.\nMacGrann's Dried Meats MacGrann's Meat Locker","desc":"I had a month's worth of dried meats salted and locked away for the cold season. Kept it locked so the bears wouldn't get it! But while I was off hunting deer, that beast, Old Icebeard, made off with the meat locker. He won't be able to smash through that Thorium though. But I'll starve if I can't get my meats back.\nYou seem a bit more stealthy than me. Perhaps you can retrieve my stash? I'll never make it in and out of that cave fast enough with this bum leg of mine.","rew":"You will be able to choose one of these rewards:\nIronwrought Bracers Wooly Mittens\nExperience: 900\n+100 reputation with Ironforge\n+100 reputation with Gnomeregan Exiles","back":"Were you able to get into my meat locker, ‹name›?","done":"What a kind soul you are, ‹name›! Thanks to your bravery I won't find myself starving when the cold season flurries blow in.","pins":[{"z":"Dun Morogh","x":34.6,"y":51.7,"n":"Tundra MacGrann","e":1,"s":1}],"cats":["dun-morogh"]},"96392":{"id":96392,"t":"Farsens watch","lv":13,"min":9,"side":"Alliance","tag":"new","st":"New in Forever.","obj":"Speak with Earthseer Farsen's and ask him to lend you his farsight to observe the Dark Iron threat.\nUse Farsen's Farsight","desc":"Greetings to ye, friend. My name is Earthseer Farsen and I'm visiting Dun Morogh from Aerie Peak. As I was travelin', I couldn't help but notice that we have, well... a bit o' a Dark Iron Dwarf problem.\nIf ye have a moment, I can show ye what I mean. I've got a bit o' magic that should do the trick.","back":"Farsight can show ye a great many things, even things ye'd rather not see.","done":"So ye see now, ‹class›? Thick as cockroaches they are, and that's just the ones we can see from the sky.\nYe look like a sturdy enough sort. Hows about a bit o' violence?","pins":[{"z":"Dun Morogh","x":64.8,"y":58.4,"n":"Earthseer Farsen","e":1,"s":1}],"cats":["dun-morogh"]},"792":{"id":792,"t":"Vile Familiars","lv":4,"min":2,"side":"Horde","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Kill 12 Vile Familiars.\nReturn to Zureetha Fargaze outside the Den.\nVile Familiar slain : 0/ 12","desc":"I trust the Valley of Trials will teach you much, young ‹class›.\nI was sent to the Valley to guide you, but I have discovered a growing taint here...\nA group that calls itself the Burning Blade has a coven here in the Valley of Trials. They are skulking in a cave to the northeast, and their Vile Familiars have spilled from its mouth to cause havoc.\nAs your first task against the Burning Blade, I bid you, defeat these familiars. Slay many and, if you survive, return to me.","rew":"You will be able to choose one of these rewards:\nPrimitive Club Primitive Hand Blade Primitive Hatchet Primitive Walking Stick\nExperience: 450\n+150 reputation with Orgrimmar\n+150 reputation with Darkspear Trolls","back":"To prove yourself against the Burning Blade, you must first defeat its Vile Familiars. Return to me when you have done this.","done":"You have done well, ‹name›.\nAlthough the Vile Familiars were merely pets of the darker powers within the Burning Blade, your success against them foretells greater deeds ahead.","pins":[{"z":"Durotar","x":42.8,"y":69.1,"n":"Zureetha Fargaze","e":1,"s":1}],"cats":["durotar"]},"72":{"id":72,"t":"The Legend of Stalvan","lv":28,"min":22,"side":"Alliance","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Search through the packed up possessions for a clue.","desc":"My father was the caretaker of the estate long before I was. He had to mop the blood up after the massacre. But that's neither here nor there.\nThe last funds of the Flintridge trust have dried up. Now the last of the family possessions are headed for auction. Blame the tax vultures. I guess if you're really itching to learn more you're free to look through this junk. Who knows what you might find.","rew":"Experience: 230","done":"You slowly slide the lid of the crate off. . . .","pins":[{"z":"Stormwind City","x":42.5,"y":72.4,"n":"Caretaker Folsom","s":1},{"z":"Stormwind City","x":42.5,"y":72,"n":"Sealed Crate","e":1}],"cats":["duskwood"]},"91752":{"id":91752,"t":"The big picture","lv":3,"min":1,"side":"Alliance","tag":"new","st":"New in Forever.","obj":"Retrieve a Sack of \"Picture\" Books from Shinyfinder Narf. Bring the sack to Marshal McBride just inside Northshire's Abbey.\nSack of \"Picture\" Books","desc":"Every once in a while, a kobold comes through yelling \"Picture for Narf!\" I don't know who Narf is. Maybe one of the head kobolds at the back of the mine? I bet he has a whole sack of books by now.\nGo get those books and bring them to our local law enforcement, Marshal McBride. You should find a friend to help. Those kobolds inside the mine are a lot meaner.","rew":"Money: 1 0 gold, 1 silver, 0 copper Experience: 320\n+100 reputation with Stormwind","back":"Have you retrieved those stolen books yet?","done":"Thank you for returning these stolen books, Jødekong. I'll get them back to Brother Paxton at once.\nYou're becoming quite the hero around here. Great job!","pins":[{"z":"Elwynn Forest","x":47.2,"y":32.2,"n":"Kelsey Fargo","s":1},{"z":"Elwynn Forest","x":48.8,"y":41.6,"n":"Marshal McBride","e":1}],"cats":["elwynn-forest"]},"2952":{"id":2952,"t":"The Sparklematic 5200!","lv":30,"min":25,"side":"Both","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","rew":"You will receive:\nSparklematic-Wrapped Box\nExperience: 2,450","done":"As quickly as it started, the Sparklematic 5200 comes to an abrupt halt. A simple \"ding\" is heard from the machine, and the mouth of the machine spirals upward. Inside the Sparklematic 5200 is a small box wrapped in a little bow. The machine would appear to wrap an object up after eliminating its grime-encrusted status. Even if the machine didn't work, at least the item is now wrapped in a pretty box.\nWell, there is one way to find out if it cleaned the item or not...\nStart The Sparklematic 5200 End The Sparklematic 5200 Level 30 , requires level 25 Difficulty 25 26 28 33 38 Side Human, Orc, Dwarf, Night Elf, Undead, Tauren, Gnome, Troll Type Dungeon Shareable Yes Quest ID 2952\nThe chain\n3 quests at level 30, 2,450 XP in all.\n1 [ 30 ] The Sparklematic 5200!\nInsert a Grime-Encrusted Item into the Sparklematic 5200, and be sure to have three silver coins to start the machine.\nThe Sparklematic 5200\n2 [ 30 ] The Sparklematic 5200! this quest\nThe Sparklematic 5200\n2,450 XP\n3 [ 30 ] More Sparklematic Action\nThe Sparklematic 5200","cats":["gnomeregan"]},"552":{"id":552,"t":"Helcular's Revenge","lv":33,"min":29,"side":"Horde","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Retrieve Helcular's Rod from the Yeti and bring it back to Novice Thaivand in Tarren Mill.\nHelcular's Rod Giant Yeti 6 % , Mountain Yeti 6 % , Ferocious Yeti 6 % , Cave Yeti 6 %","desc":"Master Helcular was almost complete with his transformation into a Lich when a human lynch mob discovered his ritual lair in the hills and brutally killed him. To make matters worse they buried his corpse in the Southshore cemetery.\nSuch disregard for the great wizard is unacceptable. As his apprentice I shall see to it that the rains of vengeance fall upon the town of Southshore.\nWe will need Helcular's Rod first. Yeti overtook his ritual lair. Undoubtedly one of the beasts has it.","rew":"Experience: 2,650\n+100 reputation with Undercity","back":"Have you recovered Helcular's Rod yet? There are so many Yeti in this region, it will be very difficult to locate. But we must have it in order to proceed.","done":"You found it! Most excellent, ‹name›!\nHillsbrad Foothills Alterac Mountains","pins":[{"z":"Hillsbrad Foothills","x":63.9,"y":19.7,"n":"Novice Thaivand","e":1,"s":1}],"cats":["hillsbrad-foothills"]},"94792":{"id":94792,"t":"Taming the beast","lv":10,"min":10,"side":"Alliance","tag":"new","st":"New in Forever.","obj":"Use the Taming Rod to tame a Rockhide Boar. Practice your skills, then return the Taming Rod to Josephine Carson.\nTame a Rockhide Boar\nProvided: Taming Rod","desc":"Many hunters prefer to travel with animal companions. With a beast at your side, you will find that you can survive even the most dangerous of circumstances. As they say, everything is easier with a friend. However, obtaining an animal companion is something that must be done with care. The balance of nature is delicate, and must always be respected.\nTake this Taming Rod with you to the forest. With it, you will be able to tame a Rockhide Boar and practice your skills as a hunter.","back":"You will learn, Darlin, and one day you will be a great ‹class›.","done":"Excellent, Darlin! You are quite a fast learner.","pins":[{"z":"Elwynn Forest","x":41.2,"y":66.2,"n":"Josephine Carson","e":1,"s":1}],"cats":["hunter"]},"6072":{"id":6072,"t":"The Hunter's Path","lv":10,"min":10,"side":"Alliance","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Speak with Dazalar in Dolanaar.","desc":"Hello, young hunter. You look to me like you are skilled enough to handle a beast and train it as your companion.\nYou must see Dazalar in Dolanaar. He can put you on the path to earning a pet of your own.","rew":"Experience: 85","done":"Yes, it is time, ‹class›.","pins":[{"z":"Teldrassil","x":58.7,"y":40.4,"n":"Ayanna Everstride","s":1},{"z":"Teldrassil","x":56.7,"y":59.5,"n":"Dazalar","e":1}],"cats":["hunter"]},"8232":{"id":8232,"t":"The Green Drake","lv":52,"min":50,"side":"Both","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Bring the Tooth of Morphaz to Ogtinc in Azshara. Ogtinc resides atop the cliffs northeast the Ruins of Eldarath.\nTooth of Morphaz Morphaz","desc":"Now I set you on a dangerous hunt to slay the green drake, Morphaz, and bring his tooth to me. Morphaz dwells deep in Temple of Atal'Hakkar, the entrance to which lies in Swamp of Sorrows.\nIf you wish to defeat him, you must not go alone. This drake is an enemy of many -- seek others who wish to destroy him.\nThe drake's tooth represents the power a hunter will find in the company of others. Bring it to me and you will have learned much.","rew":"You will be able to choose one of these rewards:\nHunting Spear Devilsaur Eye Devilsaur Tooth\nExperience: 6,350","back":"I see wisdom in your eyes, ‹name›. Has your hunt ended?","done":"You have learned the old ways, ‹name›, and for that I offer you a gift from my days as a hunter.","pins":[{"z":"Azshara","x":42.4,"y":42.6,"n":"Ogtinc","e":1,"s":1}],"cats":["hunter"]},"8952":{"id":8952,"t":"Anthion's Parting Words","lv":60,"min":58,"side":"Alliance","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Return to Deliana in Ironforge with a set of Beaststalker's Boots, Beaststalker's Pants and Beaststalker's Mantle.\nBeaststalker's Boots Nerub'enkan 0 % in Stratholme\nBeaststalker's Pants Baron Rivendare 0 % in Stratholme\nBeaststalker's Mantle Overlord Wyrmthalak 0 %\nProvided: Top Piece of Lord Valthalak's Amulet","desc":"Valthalak's soul was stored in this amulet. In our greed we foolishly split it into three parts, not knowing the curse that would await us.\nThe only way to stop Valthalak's spell is to put the medallion back together. Return to Deliana and tell her that Bodley is her only hope for finding the remaining pieces. Speak to her about any rewards you've arranged for.\nI, for once, shall rest in peace. I wish you the best of luck; you shall need every bit of it!","rew":"You will receive:\nBeastmaster's Boots Beastmaster's Pants Beastmaster's Mantle\nExperience: 9,950","back":"You're back, ‹name›. You must tell me all about what you've found out. But first let us arrange for your reward.","done":"I can't believe our lives are all but forfeit all because of a stupid medallion! And you're sure Anthion mentioned Bodley?\nWell, you've done your job so let's get your reward out of the way.\nEastern Plaguelands Dun Morogh","pins":[{"z":"Eastern Plaguelands","x":26.1,"y":11.3,"n":"Anthion Harmon","s":1},{"z":"Dun Morogh","x":58.1,"y":29.5,"n":"Deliana","e":1}],"cats":["ironforge"]},"6392":{"id":6392,"t":"Return to Brock","lv":10,"min":10,"side":"Alliance","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Buy a gryphon to Thelsamar from the gryphon master Gryth Thurden, then bring the Honorary Picks to Brock Stoneseeker in Thelsamar.\nHonorary Picks\nProvided: Honorary Picks","desc":"For a small fee you can buy a gryphon ride to Thelsamar... as long as you've already been there. Gryphons will only fly you to places you've already been, so be sure to speak with every gryphon master you see so you can fly to him later.\nYou've already been to Thorgrum, the gryphon master of Thelsamar, so now you can return to him. And once in Thelsamar, you can deliver the picks to Brock Stoneseeker.\nSpeak with me when you're ready to go.","rew":"Money: 3 50 0 gold, 3 silver, 50 copper Experience: 1,050\n+150 reputation with Ironforge\n+150 reputation with Gnomeregan Exiles","back":"Ah, ‹name›. Have you returned from Ironforge?","done":"You brought the picks. Great! I'll get these to my mining students. I'm sure they're eager to use them on the ore deposits of Loch Modan.\nThank you for your help, ‹name›. I am in your debt, but I hope this money will at least cover your travel costs.\nDun Morogh Loch Modan","pins":[{"z":"Dun Morogh","x":60,"y":28.8,"n":"Gryth Thurden","s":1},{"z":"Loch Modan","x":37,"y":47.8,"n":"Brock Stoneseeker","e":1}],"cats":["loch-modan"]},"8872":{"id":8872,"t":"The Lunar Festival","lv":60,"min":1,"side":"Alliance","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Talk to the Lunar Festival Harbinger at the Cenarion Enclave in Darnassus. You can also talk to Lunar Festival Harbingers in other capital cities.","desc":"It's that time of the year, ‹name›! The Cenarion Circle invites all denizens of Azeroth to partake in our celebration of the Lunar Festival. You will find the Lunar Festival Harbinger in this very city at a location marked by a blessed circle of moonlight. She can tell you more about the holiday.","done":"Welcome, ‹name›. Are you here to join in the festivities?\nStormwind City Dun Morogh Darnassus Tirisfal Glades Orgrimmar Thunder Bluff","pins":[{"z":"Stormwind City","x":37.1,"y":64.7,"n":"Lunar Festival Emissary","s":1},{"z":"Dun Morogh","x":55.9,"y":24,"n":"Lunar Festival Emissary","s":1},{"z":"Darnassus","x":31.2,"y":12.5,"n":"Lunar Festival Emissary","s":1},{"z":"Tirisfal Glades","x":61.7,"y":72.7,"n":"Lunar Festival Harbinger","e":1},{"z":"Orgrimmar","x":41.7,"y":32,"n":"Lunar Festival Harbinger","e":1},{"z":"Thunder Bluff","x":71.1,"y":28.2,"n":"Lunar Festival Harbinger","e":1}],"cats":["lunar-festival"]},"9112":{"id":9112,"t":"Leggings of Faith","lv":60,"min":60,"side":"Both","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Father Inigo Montoy at Light's Hope Chapel in the Eastern Plaguelands will make Leggings of Faith if you bring him the following: 1 Desecrated Leggings, 20 Wartorn Cloth Scraps, 4 Mooncloth and 2 Nexus Crystals.\nDesecrated Leggings\n20 Wartorn Cloth Scrap Stoneskin Gargoyle 35 % in Naxxramas , Infectious Ghoul 30.3 % in Naxxramas , Bile Retcher 28.5 % in Naxxramas , Mad Scientist 28.3 % in Naxxramas and 4 more\n4 Mooncloth\n2 Nexus Crystal","desc":"<Father Montoy makes some strange gestures in the air in front of you.>\nBlessed boy/girl, have you found the vestments of the fallen? The poor souls whose last breaths were taken on the field of battle - stripped of everything including their dignity.\nBring me the desecrated remnants of the departed along with reagents of purification and you shall know faith.","rew":"You will receive:\nLeggings of Faith\n+200 reputation with Argent Dawn","back":"You got some missing parts for the quest please go and get them all!","done":"Exellent ‹name› !\n, you got everything just as i asked and now i can make a Leggings of Faith.","pins":[{"z":"Eastern Plaguelands","x":71.7,"y":48.6,"n":"Father Inigo Montoy","e":1,"s":1}],"cats":["naxxramas"]},"1432":{"id":1432,"t":"Alliance Relations","lv":30,"min":30,"side":"Horde","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Speak to Takata Steelblade in Desolace.","desc":"As the Alliance progresses deeper and deeper into Kalimdor, incorrect conclusions may be drawn about the Horde making pacts with the Burning Legion. The Warchief cannot allow that to happen. And with his blessing, I am taking control of overseeing them removed.\nI have agents in the area of Desolace at the Ghost Walker Post north of the great Kodo Graveyard. Head south of the Charred Vale in the Stonetalon Mountains and you shall come across it. When you arrive, seek out Takata Steelblade.","rew":"Experience: 1,200\n+50 reputation with Orgrimmar","done":"Greetings, ‹class›. You bring news from Orgrimmar; that is good.\nThe demon infestation overwhelms this area even more than the smell of centaur dung. The horse-men claim this land as their own, but clearly there are influences out of their control that will crush them if not kept in check.\nIt does not please me that we aid the centaur indirectly, but it is for the good of the Horde, so I do my duty for the Warchief, even if it means helping the warlocks within the Horde.\nOrgrimmar Desolace","pins":[{"z":"Orgrimmar","x":22.6,"y":52.6,"n":"Keldran","s":1},{"z":"Desolace","x":52.6,"y":54.4,"n":"Takata Steelblade","e":1}],"cats":["orgrimmar"]},"7832":{"id":7832,"t":"Additional Runecloth","lv":60,"min":50,"side":"Horde","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"20 Runecloth Stormwind Royal Guard , Honor Guard , Skullsplitter Speaker in Zul'Gurub , General Marcus Jonathan 85.7 % and 4 more","back":"Greetings once again, ‹name›! Our need for runecloth is constant, and we can always use additional resources if you are willing to part with them. For an additional stack of twenty runecloth, I will make sure that you are recognized for your continuing efforts on behalf of Orgrimmar.\nWhenever you are ready to hand in the stack of runecloth, I'll accept it.","done":"‹name› - without heroes like you working on behalf of Orgrimmar, we'd surely suffer. Thank you for your continued efforts!","pins":[{"z":"Orgrimmar","x":63.6,"y":51.2,"n":"Rashona Straglash","e":1,"s":1}],"cats":["orgrimmar"]},"5672":{"id":5672,"t":"Elune's Grace","lv":20,"min":20,"side":"Alliance","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Speak to Priestess Alathea in Darnassus.","desc":"A wonderful day has come, ‹name›. You've reached the age in which our <priests or priestesses> are trained in abilities only Night elves know. But it is not for me to train you. You must return to the Temple of the Moon and speak to Priestess Alathea as soon as your business here is concluded. She will test you to ensure you're prepared, and only then will she teach you Elune's Grace.","rew":"You will learn: Elune's Grace","done":"By devoting yourself to Elune and our people, you have attained a state that not all of us can achieve. It is tradition that you then be taught even greater abilities for your devotion. Do you accept?\nTeldrassil Darnassus","pins":[{"z":"Teldrassil","x":55.6,"y":56.7,"n":"Laurna Morninglight","s":1},{"z":"Darnassus","x":39.5,"y":81.2,"n":"Priestess Alathea","e":1}],"cats":["priest"]},"8312":{"id":8312,"t":"Hallow's End Treats for Spoops!","lv":60,"min":10,"side":"Horde","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Speak with the innkeepers of Orgrimmar, Undercity, and Thunder Bluff, as well as Kali Remik in Sen'jin Village. Perform the tricks they ask of you in exchange for the treats they offer.\nReturn to Spoops at the Orgrimmar Orphanage with a Thunder Bluff Marzipan, Darkspear Gumdrop, Orgrimmar Nougat, and Undercity Mint.\nOrgrimmar Nougat\nDarkspear Gumdrop\nUndercity Mint\nThunder Bluff Marzipan","desc":"I want to go trick-or-treating, but I can't because I'm sick. If you go for me, I'd trade you the candy you get for some I already have! I think you'd like this candy - it makes you turn into things both funny and scary!\nEach of the innkeepers in the big cities have candy they give for Hallow's End - talk to them and do the tricks they ask for! Also, a troll named Kali Remik in Sen'jin Village is handing out candy as well. When you have all the candy, bring them back to me here!","rew":"You will receive:\n30 Hallow's End Pumpkin Treat\nExperience: 1,650\n+100 reputation with Horde","back":"Have you finished trick-or-treating yet? I'm sad that I can't go because I'm sick, but you helping me out makes me feel a little better...","done":"Wow, you got them all! You're awesome!\nThank you for trick-or-treating for me. Here, take these pumpkin treats - I think you'll like them a lot!\nHappy Hallow's End, ‹name›!\nOrgrimmar Durotar Thunder Bluff Tirisfal Glades","pins":[{"z":"Orgrimmar","x":71.4,"y":22.8,"n":"Spoops","e":1,"s":1}],"cats":["seasonal"]},"94472":{"id":94472,"t":"Earth sapta","lv":4,"min":4,"side":"Alliance","tag":"new","st":"New in Forever.","obj":"Speak to Teo Hammerstorm for another Earth Sapta.","rew":"You will receive:\nEarth Sapta","done":"Take this and remember, it is sacred.","pins":[{"z":"Dun Morogh","x":28.7,"y":66.1,"n":"Teo Hammerstorm","e":1,"s":1}],"cats":["shaman"]},"392":{"id":392,"t":"The Curious Visitor","lv":29,"min":16,"side":"Alliance","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Bring the Sealed","desc":"of Thredd's Visitor to Baros Alexston in Stormwind.\nSealed Description of Thredd's Visitor\nProvided: Sealed Description of Thredd's Visitor\nDescription\nDuring the first years of Thredd's imprisonment, he never had any visitors. I figured that he was no longer of use to the Brotherhood, so they abandoned him.\nAnyway, a few months ago, that all changed; he started to get regular visits... once, maybe twice a week. It was a strange man--the quiet type. I had my suspicions, but all his papers checked out.\nHis documents claimed his name was Maelik; here's his description. I don't think he'll be coming to visit Thredd anymore.","rew":"Experience: 600\n+25 reputation with Stormwind","back":"Yes, ‹name›? What have you found?","done":"Hmm. Maelik? No, the name doesn't sound familiar and neither does this description. But it could be anybody! A former Stonemason, one of the Defias Brotherhood... Though if he is as well connected as Thelwater suggests, perhaps someone else might recognize him. Let me think.","pins":[{"z":"Stormwind City","x":51.5,"y":69.4,"n":"Warden Thelwater","s":1},{"z":"Stormwind City","x":57.7,"y":47.9,"n":"Baros Alexston","e":1}],"cats":["stormwind-city"]},"8552":{"id":8552,"t":"The Monogrammed Sash","lv":50,"min":35,"side":"Both","tag":"changed","st":"Changed in Forever. Requires level 35 instead of 40.","obj":"Return the Monogrammed Sash to its owner.\nMonogrammed Sash Mok'rash 86.5 %\nProvided: Monogrammed Sash","desc":"This fine sash has the letters \"HS\" embroidered along its hem.","rew":"Experience: 2,350\n+50 reputation with Booty Bay\n-250 reputation with Bloodsail Buccaneers","back":"Hello. Do you have business with me?","done":"You recovered my sash? Then... you must have killed Mok'rash the sea giant! Hooray!\nI'm glad the scurvy villain's dead - Mok'rash was one of three sea giants who smashed my ships and killed my crew.\nThree times.\nYou are a ‹class› of worth, ‹name›.","pins":[{"z":"Stranglethorn Vale","x":26.7,"y":73.6,"n":"Captain Hecklebury Smotts","e":1}],"cats":["stranglethorn-vale"]},"9272":{"id":9272,"t":"Dressing the Part","lv":55,"min":49,"side":"Both","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","rew":"You will receive:\nBuccaneer's Uniform\n+10 reputation with Bloodsail Buccaneers\n-500 reputation with Booty Bay","done":"Yarrr... if ye be keen on enjoying the company of us experienced sea dogs, you'd best belay dressing like a blaggard! Here, put on something proper 'fore I keelhaul yer hide.\nThese'll fit ye better than they ever fit that old dog, Red-Eyed Ben. Lost him in a devil of a storm at sea.\nWear 'em with pride, mate!","pins":[{"z":"Stranglethorn Vale","x":30.6,"y":90.6,"n":"Fleet Master Firallon","e":1,"s":1}],"cats":["stranglethorn-vale"]},"8072":{"id":8072,"t":"Paragons of Power: The Madcap's Mantle","lv":60,"min":58,"side":"Both","tag":"changed","st":"Changed in Forever. Requires level 58 instead of 60. Gives 6,600 experience instead of 9,550, 0.69 times as much.","obj":"Bring Falthir the Sightless a Primal Hakkari Girdle. You must also have a reputation equal to or greater than Honored with the Zandalar Tribe.\nFalthir the Sightless is located on Yojamba Isle, Stranglethorn Vale.\nPrimal Hakkari Girdle\nReach 9000 reputation with Zandalar Tribe","desc":"One of Zandalar's legendary madcaps was Khar'vaxal the Cracked. Legend states that when facing the enemies of the tribe for the first time, Kar'xavan used his mantle specifically woven with \"the weave of madness\". His form was shrouded not only by the mantle, but also with the blinding speed of his twin daggers. Madcaps today cherish their mantle as a sign of their place in the tribe.\nBring to me the Paragons of Power I seek, and such a mantle will be yours to weave madness unto your own enemies.","rew":"You will receive:\nZandalar Madcap's Mantle\nExperience: 6,600\n+150 reputation with Zandalar Tribe","back":"You've returned - do you have the Paragons of Power I need?\nThe legend of Khar'vaxal the Cracked serves us today as a reminder that no foe - no matter how great a threat they may be - is impossible to overcome. Chaos will bring everyone to their knees, that much is certain... and perhaps the most non-chaotic elements of chaos.","done":"Victory is ours this day, thanks to the madness you have sowed upon our mutual enemies! You are to be honored amongst the Zandalar, and there is no better way of showing gratitude for your deeds than by offering you the madcap's mantle!","pins":[{"z":"Stranglethorn Vale","x":14.1,"y":13.7,"n":"Falthir the Sightless","e":1,"s":1}],"cats":["stranglethorn-vale"]},"3512":{"id":3512,"t":"In Eranikus' Own Words","lv":55,"min":48,"side":"Both","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Travel to the eastern part of Winterspring and speak with Umbranse the Spiritspeaker.","desc":"‹name›, our first step will be to devise a method to speak with Eranikus through the gem. He lies in a precarious state between sleep and death now, twisted within a weave of nightmares. Though the essence you have given me is badly tainted, there is a chance we can reach him.\nTravel far to the icy lands of eastern Winterspring and seek one of our mortal allies, Umbranse the Spiritspeaker. He is a human medium who speaks for the dead. Though Eranikus is not truly dead, he may be of aid to us still.","rew":"Experience: 4,200","done":"Itharius was wise to send you to me. While he is not dead as you understand death, Eranikus will soon give us advice in his own words. For now though, I cannot directly help you... at least not yet.\nI will lend my skill at death-speaking to you, but first I need the help of one who - unlike me - is not limited by the frailties of old age. My most potent augury device has been taken from me against my will, and unless I have it back we will be at a loss to help Eranikus.\nSwamp of Sorrows Winterspring","pins":[{"z":"Swamp of Sorrows","x":13.7,"y":71.7,"n":"Itharius","s":1},{"z":"Winterspring","x":67.8,"y":27.4,"n":"Umbranse the Spiritspeaker","e":1}],"cats":["swamp-of-sorrows"]},"2872":{"id":2872,"t":"Stoley's Debt","lv":45,"min":40,"side":"Both","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Speak with Stoley in Steamwheedle Port.","desc":"My old buddy Stoley owes me a very special bottle of rum. He tends the bar at Steamwheedle Port in Tanaris, Kalimdor, and he promised me that the rum there is stronger than anything we can find in Booty Bay. He's so confident that he says if I try that rum and don't agree with him, then he'll double the money he owes me!\nWell, I think he's not as confident as he was when last we spoke, and now he's afraid to give me that rum. But I don't back down from wagers, so why don't you talk to him for me...","rew":"Experience: 390","done":"Ah, so you've been speaking with MacKinley, have you?\nIt's not what he thinks! I'm not afraid to give him some Steamwheedle Bilge Rum...\nI just don't have any rum to give him!\nStranglethorn Vale Tanaris","pins":[{"z":"Stranglethorn Vale","x":27.8,"y":77.1,"n":"\"Sea Wolf\" MacKinley","s":1},{"z":"Tanaris","x":67.1,"y":24,"n":"Stoley","e":1}],"cats":["tanaris"]},"98392":{"id":98392,"t":"Darkness in the glade","lv":12,"min":6,"side":"Alliance","tag":"new","st":"New in Forever.","obj":"Collect Hatescreech's Amulet, Windmistress Gaedress' Amulet, and Witchmother Arysa's Amulet for Sentinel Arynia Cloudsbreak in the Oracle Glade.\nHatescreech's Amulet\nWindmistress Gaedress' Amulet\nWitchmother Arysa's Amulet","desc":"These belts... look closely at the leather, ‹name›. Do you see the taint running through the fibers?\nI have a suspicion as to its origin, but we will need further proof to be sure.\nVenture back out into the harpies' nests to the west and take out their leaders. If their necklaces carry the same darkness as these belts, we'll have our answer.","back":"Have you wrested the amulets from the harpies' leaders?","done":"<Arynia investigates the amulets.>\nDo you see the foul green swirls within the gems? This is indeed fel moss corruption at work.\nI have heard similar reports from Shadowglen and elsewhere in the boughs of this substance turning our very world against us.\nI will inform my superiors of this at once.","pins":[{"z":"Teldrassil","x":38.2,"y":34.4,"n":"Sentinel Arynia Cloudsbreak","e":1,"s":1}],"cats":["teldrassil"]},"872":{"id":872,"t":"The Disruption Ends","lv":15,"min":9,"side":"Horde","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Kill 8 Razormane Geomancers, 8 Razormane Defenders, and Kreenig Snarlsnout.\nThen bring Kreenig Snarlsnout's Tusk to Thork at the Crossroads.\nKreenig Snarlsnout's Tusk Kreenig Snarlsnout\nRazormane Geomancer slain : 0/ 8\nRazormane Defender slain : 0/ 8","desc":"One of my scouts witnessed an attack on a caravan from Durotar, ‹name›. The culprits are indeed the Razormane tribe of quilboars. One of the quilboars in particular is leading the raids: Kreenig Snarlsnout. He was seen northeast of here, just south of the road from Durotar. If the threat is to be ended, then Kreenig must die.\nTo be sure the attacks cease, though, I say we add insult to their injury. Kill Kreenig along with more of their tribe, and return to me when you have his tusk.","rew":"You will be able to choose one of these rewards:\nBinding Girdle Cinched Belt\nExperience: 1,050\n+100 reputation with Orgrimmar","back":"Cut off the head of their leader, and chaos ensues, ‹name›. Learn this lesson well. It will aid you in the future.\nThe boars will flounder without direction, and we will be able to take back the Barrens.","done":"Well done, ‹name›. With Kreenig's death, there will be a definite decline in the attacks on our caravans.\nYour people should be proud to count you among them.","pins":[{"z":"The Barrens","x":51.5,"y":30.9,"n":"Thork","e":1,"s":1}],"cats":["the-barrens"]},"79192":{"id":79192,"t":"Stepping stones","lv":24,"min":14,"side":"Both","tag":"new","st":"New in Forever.","obj":"You tear the note from the plank and read the scrawled writing.","desc":"The note begins, \"Mission said they were both making deliveries for New Plague. Looks like simple apothecary accidents to me. Find my cozy spot in the mountains between The Barrens and Desolace if you want a safe place to talk.\"","rew":"You will be able to choose one of these rewards:\nMining Pick Farmer's Shovel\nYou will also receive:\nSturdy Lunchbox Simple Wood Flint and Tinder Item 221498\nExperience: 1,950","done":"Backcountry adventurers and mercenaries alike undoubtedly make camp here. The corner of a note flapping in the breeze catches your eye and you reach for it.\nThe Barrens Westfall Stonetalon Mountains","pins":[{"z":"The Barrens","x":46.4,"y":73.9,"n":"Burned-Out Remains","s":1},{"z":"The Barrens","x":46.4,"y":73.8,"n":"Nailed Plank","s":1},{"z":"Westfall","x":37.5,"y":50.7,"n":"Burned-Out Remains","s":1},{"z":"Westfall","x":37.5,"y":50.8,"n":"Nailed Plank","s":1},{"z":"Stonetalon Mountains","x":40.8,"y":52.5,"n":"Pocket Litter","e":1}],"cats":["the-barrens"]},"1112":{"id":1112,"t":"Parts for Kravel","lv":36,"min":30,"side":"Both","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Bring Kravel's Parts to Kravel Koalbeard in the Shimmering Flats.\nKravel's Parts\nProvided: Kravel's Parts","desc":"Here's Kravel's package, ‹name›. And when you deliver it, tell him... if he wants more special orders, then he'll have to pay his tab!","rew":"Money: 20 0 gold, 20 silver, 0 copper Experience: 1,400","back":"Did you make it to Ratchet and get those parts?","done":"Great, you got them! Now we need to get them to the gnomes. But first...\nLet's take out one small item...\nThe Barrens Thousand Needles","pins":[{"z":"The Barrens","x":63.4,"y":38.5,"n":"Wharfmaster Dizzywig","s":1},{"z":"Thousand Needles","x":77.8,"y":77.3,"n":"Kravel Koalbeard","e":1}],"cats":["thousand-needles"]},"1192":{"id":1192,"t":"Indurium Ore","lv":42,"min":29,"side":"Both","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"4 Indurium Ore Indurium Mineral Vein , Earthen Sculptor 0.3 % , Shadowforge Geologist 0.2 % , Venomlash Scorpid 0.2 % and 4 more","rew":"Money: 6 0 gold, 6 silver, 0 copper","back":"I'd like to integrate indurium into different parts of our racers, but I need large amounts of raw indurium to create these parts.\nYou can find indurium ore in the Uldaman excavation in the Badlands, across the sea in Khaz Modan.\nThe gnomes are getting their own supply of it, so it's important we get our own to keep pace with them.","done":"Excellent! I'll get the crew to work right away on the parts we'll need for the next race.","pins":[{"z":"Thousand Needles","x":80.2,"y":75.9,"n":"Pozzik","e":1,"s":1}],"cats":["thousand-needles"]},"3912":{"id":3912,"t":"Meet at the Grave","lv":52,"min":47,"side":"Both","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Go to the graveyard outside Gadgetzan, and use the Videre Elixir. Follow the rest of Donova's instructions to find Gaeriyan.\nProvided: Linken's Tempered Sword","desc":"This elixir will allow you to speak with one that you would not normally even see...\nTake the Videre elixir, along with Linken's sword, to the graveyard just outside Gadgetzan in Tanaris. Once there, drink the potion. You may be quite surprised at the results, but do not be alarmed.\nIn your \"other\" form, head due north until you reach the mountains. You'll find the one you need to speak with in one of the rocky crevices. His name is Gaeriyan.\nRemember, he will only speak to you in that form...","rew":"Experience: 5,100","done":"It has been long since any have come to talk with me...\nWinterspring Tanaris","pins":[{"z":"Winterspring","x":31.3,"y":45.2,"n":"Donova Snowden","s":1},{"z":"Tanaris","x":53.9,"y":23.3,"n":"Gaeriyan","e":1}],"cats":["ungoro-crater"]},"232":{"id":232,"t":"Errand for Apothecary Zinge","lv":45,"min":38,"side":"Horde","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Take the purchase order to Alessandro Luca in the Undercity.\nZinge's Purchase Order\nProvided: Zinge's Purchase Order","desc":"The Royal Apothecary Society needs your assistance. Listen closely, and both of us may profit from my plan.\nApothecary Keever in the next room may be... touched... but his research does potentially bear fruit if it were pursued by a clever researcher. Fortunately, I am such a researcher. I want you to take this purchase order to Alessandro Luca, the proprietor of Blue Moon Odds and Ends; he'll give you a testing kit. When you have it, bring it back to me and I'll outline your task in detail.","rew":"Experience: 390\n+10 reputation with Undercity","back":"Yes, and what may I assist you with? Are you here on business for the Royal Apothecary Society, or have you arrived here merely to brighten my day?","done":"Ah, Zinge needs a kit, does she? It saddens me that Zinge does not choose to grace myself with her sweet presence.\nVery well, let me procure a kit for you.","pins":[{"z":"Undercity","x":50.1,"y":68,"n":"Apothecary Zinge","s":1},{"z":"Undercity","x":58.6,"y":54.7,"n":"Alessandro Luca","e":1}],"cats":["undercity"]},"1512":{"id":1512,"t":"Love's Gift","lv":20,"min":20,"side":"Horde","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Bring the Dirt-caked Pendant to Gan'rul Bloodeye in Orgrimmar.\nDirt-caked Pendant\nProvided: Dirt-caked Pendant","desc":"Zankaja is young and beautiful. To be chained to an invalid... I will not allow her to suffer that injustice.\nLeave me, ‹name›. And thank you. I may end my life in glorious battle, instead of a lifeless husk.\nAnd please, I would ask you not to tell my mate of this... I do not want guilt on her conscience.","rew":"Experience: 390","back":"You have returned. Are you ready to battle a succubus?","done":"If you tell me that this will suffice, then I trust you, ‹name›. Allow me to clean it though... Pristine and shining, it may be even more enticing to a succubus.\nThe Barrens Orgrimmar","pins":[{"z":"The Barrens","x":43.3,"y":47.9,"n":"Grunt Dogran","s":1},{"z":"Orgrimmar","x":48.2,"y":45.3,"n":"Gan'rul Bloodeye","e":1}],"cats":["warlock"]},"3112":{"id":3112,"t":"Simple Memorandum","lv":1,"min":1,"side":"Alliance","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Read the Simple Memorandum and speak to Thran Khorman in Coldridge Valley.\nSimple Memorandum\nProvided: Simple Memorandum","desc":"While you were helping me out, this memorandum was given to me to pass on to you. Take some time to read it when you have a chance. I'm thinkin' it came from the warrior trainer Thran. Take a gander at it and go find him inside Anvilmar when you've a chance.","rew":"Experience: 40\n+50 reputation with Gnomeregan Exiles","back":"Ah, well, another memorandum from a gnome on a mission... isn't this quaint.\nNo, no, I ain't teasin' ya, little one. Gotta respect your tenacity, that much is fer sure. I'd be just as peeved if Ironforge was taken by Dark Iron dwarves, so don't be thinkin' I don't feel for your plight...","done":"Well, seein' how this is your prime directive, or whatever yer callin' it these days, I gave my word I'd do whatever I can to make sure you and yours were ready to take back your home... and that's just what I'm gonna do.\nAny time you feel yer ready, come back to good ol' Thran and I'll be happy to share my knowledge wit ya. There's some cost to me trainin' ya, but it won't be too expensive. Good luck.","pins":[{"z":"Dun Morogh","x":29.9,"y":71.2,"n":"Sten Stoutarm","s":1},{"z":"Dun Morogh","x":28.8,"y":67.2,"n":"Thran Khorman","e":1}],"cats":["warrior"]},"152":{"id":152,"t":"The Coast Isn't Clear","lv":19,"min":10,"side":"Both","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Kill 7 Tidehunters, 7 Warriors, 7 Oracles and 7 Coastrunners and return to Captain Grayson at the Westfall Lighthouse.\nMurloc Coastrunner slain : 0/ 7\nMurloc Warrior slain : 0/ 7\nMurloc Tidehunter slain : 0/ 7\nMurloc Oracle slain : 0/ 7","desc":"You probably noticed all of the shipwrecks along the coast. The Great Sea is treacherous indeed. The coast of Westfall needs to be kept clear, so that if sailors find their way to our beaches, they are safe. The Murlocs are trouble though.\nKill 7 Tidehunters, 7 Warriors, 7 Oracles and 7 Coastrunners and I will see to it that you are rewarded.","rew":"Money: 11 0 gold, 11 silver, 0 copper Experience: 1,450","back":"Kill 7 Tidehunters, 7 Warriors, 7 Oracles and 7 Coastrunners and I will see to it that you are rewarded.","done":"Well done, ‹name›. You have quite a knack for combat. Thanks to you the Coast of Westfall is a safer place.","pins":[{"z":"Westfall","x":30,"y":86,"n":"Captain Grayson","e":1,"s":1}],"cats":["westfall"]},"472":{"id":472,"t":"Fall of Dun Modr","lv":25,"min":25,"side":"Alliance","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Search for Longbraid near the town of Dun Modr.","desc":"Dun Modr has fallen to the Dark Iron Dwarves!\nMy wounds are grave, ‹class›. Most of the regiment was killed! The Dark Iron thugs attacked us before we could regroup from the Thandol Span ambush.\nOur leader, Longbraid, sounded the retreat horn. As we left the town I was hit by a stray axe in the back. All went black.\nI awoke here in Menethil but I fear for my fellow soldiers. Hope still burns within me. Perhaps Longbraid is still alive! See if you can find him near Dun Modr, ‹race›!","rew":"Experience: 1,000\n+50 reputation with Ironforge","done":"What brave ‹class› sends word from Menethil? Ah ‹name›, they call you.\nYou bring hope to a hopeless situation. 'Tis good news indeed that young Harlo survived. While fleeing he received a grievous wound. We had but little time to send him on his way on the back of the only surviving steed with the regiment.\nBut now we face a perilous situation. Dun Modr has fallen and we are but a shadow of the great regiment we once were.","pins":[{"z":"Wetlands","x":10.8,"y":55.9,"n":"Harlo Barnaby","s":1},{"z":"Wetlands","x":49.8,"y":18.3,"n":"Longbraid the Grim","e":1}],"cats":["wetlands"]},"98072":{"id":98072,"t":"Crocs of the sky","lv":27,"min":19,"side":"Both","tag":"new","st":"New in Forever.","obj":"Collect 10 Pristine Crimson Scales and bring them to James Halloran in Menethil Harbor.\n8 Pristine Crimson Scale","desc":"You're quite the go-getter! I have just one more favor to ask, if you're up for something a bit more dangerous.\nThe crocolisk trade is steady money, but they're small fish compared to what whelp scales will bring. Folks will pay top dollar for a sack of those.\nCrocs of the sky, I call 'em! There's no way my apprentice could get them--but it seems right up your alley!\nYou'll find whelps far to the east, along the Green Belt. But be careful, there's nasty orcs in those hills!\nWetlands Open the zone on the world map Level 27 , requires level 19 Difficulty 19 23 25 30 35 Side Both factions Shareable Yes Quest ID 98072\nThe chain\n3 quests from level 27 to 29, 5,750 XP in all.\n1 [ 27 ] Crocs of the Sky this quest\nCollect 10 Pristine Crimson Scales and bring them to James Halloran in Menethil Harbor.\n2,200 XP\n2 [ 29 ] Crimson Crate Delivery\nBring the Crimson Crate to Howin Kindfeather off the road to the east of Menethil Harbor.\n1,200 XP\n3 [ 29 ] Razormaw Needling\nCollect 10 Razormaw Incisors for Howin Kindfeather.\nHowin Kindfeather Wetlands\n2,350 XP","cats":["wetlands"]},"632":{"id":632,"t":"The Thandol Span","lv":31,"min":28,"side":"Alliance","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Report back to Rhag Garmason and show him the parchment you found on Rustlocke's corpse.\nDeepfury's Orders\nProvided: Deepfury's Orders","desc":"It seems as though poor Ol' Rustlocke ran into a Dark Iron ambush. You notice a parchment next to his clenched fist.\nReport the grim news to Rhag Garmason and show him what you found.","rew":"Experience: 2,500\n+100 reputation with Ironforge","back":"Any sign of Ol' Rustlocke, ‹name›?","done":"Oh my, the news is grave....","pins":[{"z":"Wetlands","x":51.3,"y":8,"n":"Ebenezer Rustlocke's Corpse","s":1},{"z":"Wetlands","x":49.9,"y":18.2,"n":"Rhag Garmason","e":1}],"cats":["wetlands"]},"92472":{"id":92472,"t":"The next step","lv":5,"min":3,"side":"Both","tag":"new","st":"New in Forever.","obj":"Report to Constable Aonda in Shen'dar Village.","desc":"One of the most pervasive threats on Zephras Isle is the Al'Aketh Cult. They are religious zealots devoted to the worship of the supposed elemental ruler of Skywall, Al'Akir the Windlord. They are brutal, single minded, and their power and ambitions are growing more deadly by the day.\nYour path will soon take you to Shen'dar Village to the south. Present yourself to Constable Aonda when you arrive. The cult threatens Shen'dar and they are in need of aid. Tell Aonda that I sent you.","done":"Aetheen sent you, then? I'll confess, you don't look like much to me, but Shen'dar Village won't turn down willing aid, much less aid sent from Elder Aetheen herself.","pins":[{"z":"Zephras Isle","x":42.6,"y":23.6,"n":"Aetheen of the Gales","s":1},{"z":"Zephras Isle","x":45.6,"y":45.4,"n":"Constable Aonda","e":1}],"cats":["zephras-isle"]}});